  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In the equation \\(2x^2-hx+2k=0,\\) the sum of the roots is \\(4\\) and the product of the roots is \\(-3.\\) Then \\(h\\) and \\(k\\) have the values, respectively:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(8\\) and \\(-6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\) and \\(-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-3\\) and \\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-3\\) and \\(8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(8\\) and \\(-3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By Vieta’s formulas, the sum and product of the roots are \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac h2&=4,\\\\ \\frac{2k}{2}&=k=-3. \\end{aligned} \\] Hence \\(h=8\\) and \\(k=-3.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Apply Vieta’s formulas without first solving the quadratic",
        "The sum is \\(\\frac{h}{2}\\) and the product is \\(k\\)"
      ],
